cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GNNarrate: LLM-generated narratives for graph neural network
  explanations in precision medicine
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this repository and
  the CLARUS paper listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdullah M.
    family-names: Bishara
repository-code: https://github.com/abdullahbishara/gnnarrate
abstract: >-
  A narration layer for graph neural network explainability. GNNarrate
  converts the raw explanation logs produced by the CLARUS platform --
  node and edge relevance scores, prediction confidence deltas after
  counterfactual graph edits, and retraining metrics -- into plain-language
  causal explanations for each patient, aimed at clinicians and biomedical
  researchers rather than machine learning practitioners.
keywords:
  - explainable AI
  - graph neural networks
  - large language models
  - precision medicine
  - counterfactual explanation
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      CLARUS: An interactive explainable AI platform for manual
      counterfactuals in graph neural networks
    authors:
      - given-names: Jacqueline Michelle
        family-names: Metsch
      - given-names: Anna
        family-names: Saranti
      - given-names: Alessa
        family-names: Angerschmid
      - given-names: Bastian
        family-names: Pfeifer
      - given-names: Vanessa
        family-names: Klemt
      - given-names: Andreas
        family-names: Holzinger
      - given-names: Anne-Christin
        family-names: Hauschild
    journal: Journal of Biomedical Informatics
    year: 2024
    url: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1532046424000182
